2026-08-01 — build 1033 (v1.2.2)
Speed, and photos the way you shot them:
- The feed is much faster to open. It was making 106 separate requests to the
  server on every load; it now makes 46, because profiles and settings were
  being fetched over and over instead of once.
- Photos load far quicker and use a fraction of the data. Each one is now sent
  at the size your screen actually needs instead of full resolution — measured
  at about a quarter of the bytes, and in a newer format where supported.
- Reactions, comments and scrolling feel quicker as a result. They were never
  slow themselves; they were waiting behind everything else.
- YOUR PHOTO KEEPS ITS OWN SHAPE. Every upload used to be force-cropped to 4:5
  and the crop was permanent — the original never reached us. Post whatever
  shape you shot: wide, square, tall. Cropping is now optional, per photo.
- Very wide or very tall photos get a soft blurred edge instead of being cut.
- Reach and Viewed-by now appear on every post, on the same line as reactions.
- Consistent spacing under the name on every card, with or without a caption.
